Port of macos/Sources/MalachiMail/Preferences/CalendarPaneViewController.swift
(loadView, buildDisplay); GTK: none yet (Swift-first, the structure is
ui/internal/calendar/preferences.go PreferencesLayout, Core's Cal.Prefs).
Preferences → Calendar (the owner's decision of 2026-10-16, docs/calendar.md
§5.8 "As built (M9)"), one scrolling page clamped to the Preferences'
width: the group Display (Week Starts On, Default Duration, Default Alert,
Show Declined Events, Working Hours as a start and an end at half hours
with its subtitle, then the working days as seven toggle buttons under the
working hours' summary), its refusal under its heading and the write under
way beside it; then a section per account with the calendar capability
(CalendarAccountSection, made in code); the empty state "No calendars
